ang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":252},{"base":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","tr":"mil·cha·mah","gloss":"battle","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":319},{"base":"H2416","lemma":"חַי","tr":"chay","gloss":"alive","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":498},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":820}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"I tore the kingdom away from the house of David and gave it to you. But you have not been like My servant David, who kept My commandments and followed Me with all his heart, doing only what was right in My eyes.","from":5},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I will give one tribe to his son, so that My servant David will always have a lamp before Me in Jerusalem, the city where I chose to put My Name.","from":4},{"book":"2SA","chapter":11,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"In the letter he wrote: “Put Uriah at the front of the fiercest battle; then withdraw from him, so that he may be struck down and killed.”","from":5},{"book":"2SA","chapter":11,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"And when the men of the city came out and fought against Joab, some of Davidʼs servants fell, and Uriah the Hittite also died.","from":5},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For when Solomon grew old, his wives turned his heart after other gods, and he was not wholeheartedly devoted to the LORD his God, as his father David had been.","from":3},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"There was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam throughout their days.","from":6},{"book":"2CH","chapter":21,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Yet the LORD was unwilling to destroy the house of David, because of the covenant He had made with David, and since He had promised to maintain a lamp for David and his descendants forever.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"I will make you into a great nation, and I will bless you; I will make your name great, so that you will be a blessing.","from":4}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":5},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":3}]},"9-24":{"people":[{"id":"asa-h0609g","name":"Asa","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":11,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"jeroboam-h3379g","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"maacah-h4601k","name":"Maacah","kind":"person","brief":"Daughter of Uriel","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"absalom-h0053","name":"Absalom","kind":"person","brief":"David's son","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"baasha-h1201","name":"Baasha","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":5,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"ben-hadad-h1130g","name":"Ben-hadad","kind":"person","brief":"Syrian king","count":2,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"hezion-h2383","name":"Hezion","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Tabrimmon","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"tabrimmon-h2886","name":"Tabrimmon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hezion","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"naphtali-h5321g","name":"Naphtali","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":